[{"author":"coderabbitai[bot]","body":"\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai --\u003e\n\u003c!-- walkthrough_start --\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e📝 Walkthrough\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai --\u003e\n\n## Release Notes\n\n- Theme system\n  - Added ColorTheme protocol, ConfigurableTheme (JSON themes), ThemeRegistry (management + hot-reload).\n  - Bundled themes: System, Gruvbox, Gruvbox Light, Tokyo Night, Solarized Light.\n  - Custom themes load/save and file-watching via ~/.config/bat-mon/themes.json.\n\n- Menu bar \u0026 display\n  - Added four menu layouts: Native, Rich, Minimal, TUI (selectable in settings).\n  - New display formats: percentage, leftOnly, rightOnly, lowest; experimental renderers (pipes, blocks, bracketed, arrows, slashes).\n  - Compact-mode icon options and SF Symbol picker for custom menu icons.\n  - BatIconView for disconnected state (accent-based colors, thinner border by default).\n\n- Reconnect \u0026 Bluetooth UX\n  - Improved reconnect flow: caches previously selected keyboard/peripheral so it remains available after disconnect.\n  - Bluetooth scanning refinements, clamped battery percentage to [0,100], and forgetSelectedKeyboard support.\n\n- Widget \u0026 integration\n  - WidgetKit integration with app-group storage and timeline reloads; preferences now persist widget theme/layout keys.\n  - Removed legacy selectedKeyboardID persistence.\n\n- Settings \u0026 polish\n  - Settings copy/controls improved, live previews for layouts/themes, settings wiring updated.\n  - Launch-at-login utility added.\n  - macOS deployment target bumped to 14.0.\n  - Replaced print logging with os.log for better diagnostics.\n\n- Model \u0026 API changes\n  - BatteryLevel simplified: removed isCharging and visualBar.\n  - ConnectionState gained isBluetoothUnavailable computed property.\n  - AppSettings expanded with migration from legacy MenuStyle → new menuLayout + colorThemeId.\n\n- Documentation \u0026 governance\n  - Added README, BATMON_PROJECT_PLAN.md, bat-mon-PRD.md and MIT LICENSE.\n  - Info.plist now uses $(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION) and $(MARKETING_VERSION).\n  - Updated repository URL and app group identifier in constants.\n\nDidactic notes (short)\n- Theme architecture: use a protocol (ColorTheme) to define theme tokens so both static (compile-time) themes and dynamic JSON-configurable themes implement the same surface. ThemeRegistry then composes hardcoded + custom themes and exposes lookups and hot-reload—this keeps UI code theme-agnostic.\n- Reconnect caching: persist a lightweight mapping of selected keyboard → peripheral info on disconnect, surface it immediately in the UI, and attempt BLE reconnection in the background. This avoids blocking the UI on a fresh BLE scan and improves perceived reliability.\n\n| Author        | Lines Added | Lines Removed |\n|---------------|-------------:|--------------:|\n| Paolo Papania | 8,754       | 0             |\n\n\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai --\u003e\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a full theming system (built-in + JSON-configurable), major Menu Bar UI refactor with four layout styles, WidgetKit synchronization, custom theme loader with file watching, expanded preferences/settings and icon picker, Bluetooth manager enhancements, project docs/packaging updates, and assorted utilities/resources.\n\n## Changes\n\n|Cohort / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Project docs \u0026 metadata** \u003cbr\u003e `BATMON_PROJECT_PLAN.md`, `bat-mon-PRD.md`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`|Added comprehensive project plan, PRD, user README with install/theming guidance, and MIT license.|\n|**Xcode project \u0026 resources** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`, `BatMon/Resources/Info.plist`, `BatMon/Resources/Assets.xcassets/...`|Rewired project file to register new theme and utility sources, bumped macOS target to 14.0, switched Info.plist version keys to build variables, and added asset catalog (menu bar icon).|\n|**App entry \u0026 lifecycle** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/App/BatMonApp.swift`, `BatMon/App/AppDelegate.swift`|Initialize ThemeRegistry at startup, rewire MenuBarLabel to use PreferencesManager, add theme-aware menu bar rendering and new display formats, and improve logging/notification permission handling.|\n|**Theming core** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Theme/ColorTheme.swift`, `BatMon/Theme/ThemeEnvironment.swift`, `BatMon/Theme/MenuLayout.swift`, `BatMon/Theme/ThemeRegistry.swift`, `BatMon/Theme/ConfigurableTheme.swift`|Introduce ColorTheme protocol, environment modifier, menu layout enum, ThemeRegistry singleton aggregating hardcoded + custom themes, and ConfigurableTheme with JSON parse/serialize and color utilities.|\n|**Built-in themes** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Theme/Themes/*` \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Theme/Themes/SystemTheme.swift`, `.../GruvboxTheme.swift`, `.../GruvboxLightTheme.swift`, `.../TokyoNightTheme.swift`, `.../SolarizedLightTheme.swift`|Added several concrete ColorTheme implementations (System, Gruvbox, Gruvbox Light, Tokyo Night, Solarized Light).|\n|**Custom theme management** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Theme/CustomThemeLoader.swift`|Singleton loader for `~/.config/bat-mon/themes.json` with validation, save/add/update/remove operations, default initialization, and filesystem watch support.|\n|**Settings \u0026 appearance UI** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Views/Settings/SettingsView.swift`, `BatMon/Views/Settings/SFSymbolPicker.swift`|Expanded Settings with Appearance section, live theme/layout previews, theme editor flow, icon picker sheet, and related UI components.|\n|**Menu bar UI \u0026 components** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Views/MenuBar/MenuBarView.swift`, `BatMon/Views/MenuBar/BatIconView.swift`|Large rewrite adding four menu styles (Native, Rich, Minimal, TUI), many reusable view components, BatIconView vector silhouette with border options, and theme-aware visuals.|\n|**Models \u0026 migration** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Models/AppSettings.swift`, `BatMon/Models/BatteryLevel.swift`, `BatMon/Models/ConnectionState.swift`|Expanded AppSettings with layout/theme/icon/display options and migration from legacy MenuStyle; removed `isCharging`/`visualBar` from BatteryLevel; added `isBluetoothUnavailable` to ConnectionState.|\n|**Managers \u0026 WidgetKit** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Managers/BluetoothManager.swift`, `BatMon/Managers/PreferencesManager.swift`|BluetoothManager: improved scanning/connection lifecycle, caching for quick reconnect, and writes widget data; PreferencesManager: app-group persistence for widget keys and WidgetCenter reload on save.|\n|**Utilities** \u003cbr\u003e `BatMon/Utilities/Constants.swift`, `BatMon/Utilities/LaunchAtLogin.swift`|Added widget UserDefaults keys, appGroup identifier, dynamic bundle version helpers, updated GitHub URL, and LaunchAtLogin helper for login-item management.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n\u003e \u003e⎯⎯\\  \n\u003e I’m a rabbit who hops through color schemes bright,  \n\u003e nibbling Gruvbox crumbs by Tokyo night light,  \n\u003e I watch themes reload, and widgets hum along,  \n\u003e the menu bar sings — a soft batty song,  \n\u003e hop, tweak, save — the palette feels just right. 🐇✨\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- walkthrough_end --\u003e\n\n\n\u003c!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start --\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e❌ Failed checks (1 warning)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n|     Check name     | Status     | Explanation                                                                           | Resolution                                                                         |\n| :----------------: | :--------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | :-------------------------